  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: config_006, scvi_n200/multiprofile/transformer at 0.653), while image-only models are very weak (~0.21-0.23), suggesting image features carry little standalone signal. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the image modality provides any complementary information when fused with the strong RNA representation. This experiment (config_039) directly tests that question by combining the best-known RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) with the best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) using weighted fusion, which is appropriate given the large modality strength imbalance. If it exceeds 0.653, multimodal fusion is worthwhile and we can explore fusion strategies; if it does not, we can confidently focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinement. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the central design question (is multimodality useful here?) with the strongest available components, rather than testing a weaker combination that would be harder to interpret."
}

